                                "sense_id": "101e2ccb-d6c1-3c16-aea8-3798c2c4011d",
                                "text": "For toposes were invented by Grothendieck in the sixties for specific purposes in algebraic geometry and algebraic topology. Later on, Lawvere and Tierney [11] axiomatized the notion of an elementary topos with the goal of providing an appropriate foundation for differential geometry."
